+## Option Groups
+
+A command with many options is easier to read when related options are listed together. Give an option a
+`help_group`, and the help page lists it in a section of that name, after the `Options` section that holds the options
+without a group (`--help` among them):
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command(help_group_order=["Network", "Output"])
+    @click.option("--verbose", is_flag=True, help="Say more.")
+    @click.option("--color", is_flag=True, help="Use colors.", help_group="Output")
+    @click.option("--host", default="localhost", help="Server host.", help_group="Network")
+    @click.option("--port", type=int, default=80, help="Server port.", help_group="Network")
+    def serve(verbose, color, host, port):
+        pass
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(serve, args=["--help"])
+```
+
+The groups follow `help_group_order` of the command; groups that are not listed there follow in the order their first
+option appears. The second column starts at the same place in every section, so the page reads as one table.
+{meth}`Command.get_help_groups` returns the rows of each section, for a custom {meth}`Command.format_options`.
+
+The subcommands of a {class}`Group` can be grouped the same way: a command with `help_group="Admin"` is listed in an
+`Admin` section after the `Commands` section, and the group's `help_group_order` orders these sections too.
+
+```python
+@click.group(help_group_order=["Admin"])
+def cli():
+    pass
+
+@cli.command(help_group="Admin")
+def migrate():
+    """Migrate the database."""
+```
+
 ## Help Parameter Customization
 
 Help parameters are automatically added by Click for any command. The default is `--help` but can be overridden by the context setting {attr}`~Context.help_option_names`. Click resolves conflicts automatically: an option reusing one of the help option names takes it over, and the default help parameter is dropped once all its names are taken. A parameter merely named `help`, like `click.argument("help")`, does not disable it: both keep working independently.
