+## The Text of a Prompt
+
+{func}`prompt` and {func}`confirm` build the text they show with {class}`PromptText`: the question, then the choices
+of a {class}`Choice` type in parentheses, then the default in brackets, then the suffix.
+
+```python
+>>> click.PromptText("Group by", type=click.Choice(["day", "week"]), show_default=True, default="day").render()
+'Group by (day, week) [day]: '
+>>> click.PromptText.for_confirm("Continue?", default=True).render()
+'Continue? [Y/n]: '
+```
+
+Each part comes from its own method (`choices_part`, `default_part`), so a subclass can change one part and keep the
+others. This is useful to show the same text in your own messages, for example in a log of what was asked.
 
